WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.390
Coming!

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.710
Who could it be,
this early?

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.340
Huh? Ms. Junsa?

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.760
Is Director Sakuragi here?

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.970
Good morning.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.170
Is there a problem?

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:44.060
Actually, we’re here to ask about a case that’s been
taking place here in Kuchiba City over the last few days.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.690
A case?!

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.180
The detective in charge
will tell you more.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.940
With me is the chief investigator
assigned to the case, Detective Decker.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.320
Howdy there.
Call me Decker.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.080
Sorry there ‘bout callin’ so early.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.580
I’m Sakuragi, the Director.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.310
Oh, don’tcha worry,
I ain’t gonna take your time.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.160
If y’all gonna be cooperatin’,
we’ll be gone lickety-split.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.750
Of course. Ask away.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.940
Coppa relief!
Now ‘at’s good news.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.960
Well ‘en,
let’s get right down to it.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:19.470
Can ya gather up all the Electric-type Pokémon
ya got at Sakuragi Park?

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.110
Gather all the...

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:22.610
...Electric types?

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.510
‘Bout what I’d expect from
the Sakuragi Institute.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.480
Quite the lineup ya got there.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.410
What exactly is this?

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.950
Just a formality, is all.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.080
Something kinda
feels awful about this.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.250
Yeah.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.810
I knew it.
No doubtin’ it, the culprit...

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.480
...was you!

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.070
Pikachu?!

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.580
The culprit?!

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.330
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.120
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.630
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.500
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.010
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.630
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:45.560
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:50.560
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:55.070
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.490
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:04.990
I've got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:11.210
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:15.460
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.800
Let's have a fight!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.210
1. Once the battle's done

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.340
2. And we're laughing or crying

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.100
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:32.190
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:37.440
With this unpredictable, unfathomable world awaiting

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.860
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:44.030
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.780
I choose you!

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.800
Pikachu the Suspect?!

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.300
9:23 am,
suspect apprehended.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.760
Ya have the right to remain silent,
and the right to consult an attorney—

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.250
H-Hold on a minute!

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.280
Why’re you arresting Pikachu?!

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.880
Pikachu hasn’t done anything wrong!

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.980
You’re Pikachu’s trainer, ‘en?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.910
We’ve got a witness!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.130
A witness?

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.560
Ms. Junsa, what’s going on here?

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.690
Actually...

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:26.200
There’s been a string of cases of
electricity being stolen from houses in Kuchiba City.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.160
Electricity being stolen?

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.350
The power suddenly cuts out during the night,

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:34.590
and whenever we check, we keep finding
abnormal amounts of power consumption.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:41.050
A task force was formed to solve the mystery of the case,
led by Detective Decker.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:48.000
We haven’t been able to find any clues,
but we have had valuable witness testimony...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.970
I followed the footsteps I heard.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.900
Then for a moment, I saw a fleeing Pokémon,
illuminated by a car’s headlights.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:01.980
And here’s the sketch we drew up
from his testimony.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.970
That’s... Pikachu?

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:07.040
It does kinda look like one...

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.620
But still, it could be
another Pikachu.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:15.860
We’ve been lookin’ at this city’s Electric types,
‘specially the Pikachu.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.880
And we gathered that
each a’ the Pikachu’s got an alibi.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.970
‘Cept for this Institute’s one here.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.340
Alibis?

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.960
Then my Pikachu has one, too!

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.930
We’ve always been together!

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:33.640
Let me tell ya, the last theft
was at 11 pm, last night.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.800
What were ya doin’ at that time?

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.400
...I was fast asleep.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.710
Asleep?!

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:45.360
So ya sayin’ ya’d never’ve known
if Pikachu snuck out and stole electricity.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.820
But...

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.150
Detective Decker,
isn’t arresting him a bit extreme?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.740
We should rule out
any other possibilities firs—

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:58.200
My dear Junsa, I’m tellin’ ya!
My cop’s instinct is never wrong!

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.000
He’s bein’ arrested!

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.240
Ya got any more objections,
save ‘em for the station.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.470
Cop yaself a break...

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.980
‘Fess up already!

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.230
Don’tcha give me that “Pikaaa...”!

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.900
Well, how’s about this?

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.390
Ya must be starving.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:32.500
Have a bowl a’ Pokémon food.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:44.920
The sun’s shinin’...
Beautiful day out there...

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:50.430
Hey, ya got a mom waitin’ for ya
atcha hometown, don’tcha?

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:56.860
Confessin’ to yer crimes and makin’ up for ‘em’d
make her happy, ya know?

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.060
Hey, ya even listenin’ there?!

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.730
Yer supposed ta <i>spit it out!</i>
Spit it out, not fill yer belly!

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.640
He’s acting like Pikachu’s a criminal!

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.530
Something’s really wrong here!

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:17.080
Ms. Junsa, do you think
Pikachu’s the thief, too?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:23.170
No... I know Satoshi and his Pikachu.
I can’t imagine he’d do this.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.850
Then let him go!

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:30.350
But... Fact is that the sketch
is our only clue.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:33.220
Detective Decker’s been put in charge
of the investigation,

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.200
and he can jump
to conclusions at times.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:40.560
You’d need to show him some evidence
that Pikachu wasn’t behind it to clear his name...

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.430
Evidence...

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.320
Wh-What?
Whatcha tryin’ ta say?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.850
What is it, Pikachu?!

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.300
He’s acting weird.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.450
Let’s go check on him.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.250
Pikachu!

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:57.830
Hey! Where are you going?!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.370
Ya ain’t gonna cop outta this!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.290
Guardie! After him!

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.290
Suspect has fled police custody!
Follow him!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.380
Where is he going?

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:18.680
Is there something in this house?

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.030
Ya got nowhere ta run.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.650
Thief! Electricity thief!

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:28.810
What’s wrong?

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.230
Oh, Ms. Junsa!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:35.760
About ten minutes ago, the TV suddenly went off,
and my PC and fridge stopped running.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:39.510
When I checked the meter,
there was a huge amount of power being used!

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:41.590
Someone’s stealing my electricity!

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:42.780
What?!

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.420
Ms. Junsa, isn’t this...

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:48.420
Yes. There’s no mistaking it.
That’s the MO of the serial electricity thief!

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:52.190
Ten minutes ago,
Pikachu was at the police station.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.020
In other words...!

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:54.990
Pikachu has an alibi!

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:59.050
All right!
That’s great news, Pikachu!

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:00.830
I knew it.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:04.120
Ya find true culprits
in the darndest places.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.120
My instinct’s never wrong!

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.570
But all this time
you were saying Pikachu did it, yeah?

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:13.320
The thief must still be nearby.
Let’s look for them!

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.330
They gave us the slip!

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.000
They’ve always been
stealin’ at night before.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.830
Now they’re doin’ it in broad daylight,
and still leavin’ no clues!

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.240
No, Detective Decker.
We did find a clue.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:31.960
Huh?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:37.080
When the theft occurred, Pikachu reacted to something
and ran to the crime scene.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.100
Isn’t it possible he was sensing
the electricity being stolen?

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.350
What?!

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.350
Did you, Pikachu?

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:49.610
If we add Pikachu to the investigation team,
he may help us arrest the real thief!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.970
Pikachu on the
investigation team?!

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.690
Okay, got it.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:10:00.150
Pikachu’s joinin’ the case
as a special agent!

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:05.960
My dear Junsa, start up a thorough search
with Pikachu helpin’!

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:06.870
Yes, Sir!

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.890
Wow, Ms. Junsa! Can I help, too?!

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:11.650
Oh, me too!

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.170
Sarunori, too!

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.820
Let’s start by patrolling this area.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:24.250
We’re counting on you!

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:24.930
Right!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.600
Hehe, they even let us
borrow the uniforms!

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.450
It feels like we’re
real police officers!

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:34.510
I’ve always wanted to try this.

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:35.900
Yeah, me too!

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.530
You’ve nowhere to run!

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:42.120
Pokémon Kidnapper,
you’re under arrest!

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.370
I’ve worked out all the tricks.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.370
The truth is in my hands!

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.250
The culprit...

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:51.630
...was you!

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:55.750
Ms. Junsa!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:56.700
What is it?

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:59.650
My Rokon disappeared!

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:00.970
A kidnapping?!

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.590
All right,
I’ll catch the kidnapper!

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.310
Leave it to me!
The truth is in my hands!

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.750
Or wait, right now we’re busy
looking for the electricity thief...

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.830
Oh, that’s right...

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:11.810
No...

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:16.050
Helping citizens in need is also
an important duty for police officers!

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.010
Right!

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:21.230
There’s tons of Rokon...

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:24.280
I couldn’t find it
out of all the others...

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.690
Can you tell us any way to
identify your Rokon?

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:30.120
Its tail looks like a heart.

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:34.360
You hear that?
Let’s check each and every Rokon.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.380
Right!

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:47.220
I give up... I can’t find it...

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.270
Huh?
Where are Pikachu and Sarunori?

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.570
That’s it!

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:58.360
I’m so happy!
This is my Rokon!

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:00.570
Thank you!

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.670
Take care!

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:04.150
That was hard work...

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.070
...but I’m glad we found it.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.500
Ms. Junsa!

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.080
What’s wrong?

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.410
You’re nearly there!

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.090
Thank you!

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.840
You there riding the Dodrio, stop!

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.390
Satoshi, Go, follow them!

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.040
R-Right!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.420
Don’t ride Pokémon in cities!
It’s dangerous.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.030
Let alone riding double.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:36.070
Sorry...

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.310
I never knew Ms. Junsa
was so busy...

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.990
And with so many
mundane tasks...

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.850
Making sure everyone can live their lives happily
is a police officer’s job.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:02.420
Having you two with me today
has been a great help, though!

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:07.130
But we haven’t had any luck
finding the all-important electricity thief...

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:12.030
What is it, Pikachu?

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:14.280
Let’s go!

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:18.240
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:32.730
So you looked at the meter
and realized electricity was being stolen, correct?

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:36.000
Did you see anyone suspicious,
human or Pokémon?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.840
No...
I think they’d already run off...

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.770
They’re fast at getting away...

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:43.130
Pikachu had even sensed them...

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:50.100
Even if Pikachu detects a theft,
there’ll always be time lost getting to the scene.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.890
If only we could get there first
and lie in wait...

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:54.710
Lie in wait...

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:56.850
Oh, that’s it!

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.980
The thief targets houses
that use lots of power.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:06.280
So let’s have Pikachu discharge lots of electricity
at some house, and lure the thief in!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.560
I get it!

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.070
That certainly seems worth a try.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.260
Okay! Let’s do it, Pikachu.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:14.220
But whose house
do we lure them to?

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.870
Uhh... Well...

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:19.500
Why our house?

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.460
Oh, we just happened to be
in the neighborhood...

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.100
We would appreciate
your cooperation!

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.880
Well, if we can be of help...

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.930
Sorry, but just go along
with it, okay?

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:33.970
Sure, but...
What are we supposed to do?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:36.120
You don’t need to do anything.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:36.890
Huh?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.420
Okay! Let’s begin, Pikachu!

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.990
Ooh! Awesome!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.460
What is this?!

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:03.570
Go, is something wrong?

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:07.130
Is this sketch really a Pikachu?

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:10.790
Pikachu don’t have any habit
of sucking up electricity...

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:13.300
What Pokémon wants electricity...?

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.560
Dedenne!

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.520
Yeah! It does kinda
look like a Dedenne!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:24.520
We thought the same thing,
but every Dedenne nearby turned out to have an alibi.

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:27.670
Huh... Then it really is a Pikachu?

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.400
Or is it some other Pokémon?

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:36.290
Ooh, that house looks like
it’s overflowing with electricity.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.330
We’ll be able to get
lots of power here.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.590
Today is looking up, meow...

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:43.510
Finally we can get some proper food...

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:48.420
That thing’s the reason
we’ve ended up like this...

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.300
No way!

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.940
Our month’s supply of food...

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.830
We’ll end up all shriveled
if this keeps happening...

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.730
Anything but that...

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.230
I know.
Morpeko’s an Electric type, right?

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:10.100
So if we let it feast on electricity,
then it wouldn’t have room for our food, right?

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:10.990
Right.

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:13.850
Let’s get lots of electricity, meow!

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:19.670
And that’s how this
electricity vacuum car was born, meow!

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:24.250
It’s all thanks to me that we’ve been able
to steal so much electricity, meow!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:29.510
But how come every time we get back
to the hideout, the car’s empty?

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:32.410
It’s an electric car,
so there’s no getting around it, meow.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:36.010
How come we’re always using up
the electricity we steal on the road home?!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:40.180
Well, today we just have to feed it
the electricity straight away...

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.310
Hey, it looks like it’s <i>really</i> hungry...

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.890
Better get the power quick, meow.

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:00.670
Static?!

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:03.410
Whoa, electricity’s amazing!

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:03.410
No!!!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.920
The power... went out?

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:11.550
Is this...?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.430
It filled up in an instant, meow.

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:21.220
What a great feeling!
Now to feed it to Morpeko right a...

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.180
Huh? Where’s Morpeko?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.500
Ah! Morpeko!

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:35.250
What’s it doing here?

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:36.860
It ran off!

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:38.950
There you are.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.350
Were you stealing food again?

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:42.750
What’d you do that for?!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.760
We’re out here stealing electricity
to feed you...!

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.210
So that’s it!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.080
Team Rocket!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.510
Brat cop boys?!

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:51.590
I understand.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:56.840
The Pokémon the witness saw
wasn’t a Pikachu, but a Morpeko!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.810
You’re under arrest
for the crime of electricity-theft!

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:04.950
You think we’re gonna go peacefully?!

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:06.060
See ya!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:06.850
Hey, stop!

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:08.100
We’re off!

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:16.590
This is Junsa. I’m in pursuit of
the electricity thieves’ car.

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:19.700
What?!
Aight, I’ll be right there!

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.920
Come on, driving is gonna
waste the electricity!

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:25.240
Can’t you do something about
that patrol car?!

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:27.310
I’ll hit them with lightning, meow!

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.900
Just keep some for Morpeko!

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:32.090
And meow! And meow!

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:34.520
Guardie!

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:35.710
Speed Star!

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.470
We shook ‘em off, meow.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.070
Serves them right!

00:18:56.320 --> 00:19:00.980
Here you are, Morpeko.
Suckle on this to your heart’s content.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.980
We’ll keep it coming.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:06.700
Leave the food for us, meow.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:13.670
It’s not interested?
But it’s an Electric type!

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:16.170
Wh-Why? How come?

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.640
Well, duh.

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:23.680
Morpeko creates electricity, which makes it hungry,
so it fills back up by eating.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.150
Really?

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:28.050
Anyway, how come you didn’t
tell us that earlier?!

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:30.450
Huh? You never asked...

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:32.940
You’re such a...

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:35.570
We’ve found you!

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:39.090
You made people think
Pikachu was a criminal!

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:42.700
Whatever. We give up.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:46.700
We don’t need no electricity.
You can have it all back!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.580
Take this, meow.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.010
Pikachu!

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:07.450
Did he just soak up the electricity
and power up?!

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:10.730
All right, Pikachu!
200,000 Volts payback time!

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.190
Step on it!

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.890
What an awful feeling...

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:27.870
Wh-What the cop...?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.930
A certificate of appreciation,
for Pikachu.

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:40.090
We would like to express
our deepest appreciation...

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.110
...in recognition of your
exceptional contributions...

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:45.510
...in the solving of this case.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:47.970
Thank ya, honest.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:54.810
Congrats, Pikachu!

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.240
Thank you.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:05.160
Satoshi and Go,
we appreciate your cooperation, too!

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:07.430
Oh, it was a lot of fun!

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.410
We really got a taste of
how hard Ms. Junsa’s job is...

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:12.210
Here’s my cop’s intuition!

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:17.580
This Pikachu’s gonna become
an official agent, and my partner!

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:23.640
So? Wanna try yer hand
at the hardest of cases?

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:24.760
I could call you...

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.010
Coppa lotta damage!

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:37.030
Pikachu, Satoshi, and Go successfully
managed to solve a case with Junsa.

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:42.400
The peace of Kuchiba City rests on their shoulders...
Well, perhaps.

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.570
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:10.880
Go!

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:12.450
Lizardon!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:13.830
Fushigidane!

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:21.630
Of course,
who else could it be but Satoshi.

00:23:21.630 --> 00:23:23.140
Shigeru!

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:26.010
By the way, Shigeru,
what was that goal you mentioned?

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:28.490
The Legendary Pokémon, Fire.

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:29.300
Fire?

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:31.290
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.290 --> 00:23:34.350
A Rival for Go?!
The Path to Mew!!
